Subject: [PATCH] statically link libstdc++ and libgcc

As a host tool, patchelf runs directly on the build machine rather
than through any sysroot or RPATH Buildroot sets up for target
binaries, so it depends on the build machine having a dynamic
libstdc++.so.6 on its default linker search path. NixOS doesn't put
shared libraries there at all — every path is a hashed store path —
so the freshly built host-patchelf binary fails with "error while
loading shared libraries: libstdc++.so.6: cannot open shared object
file". Link libstdc++ and libgcc statically so the binary doesn't
depend on finding them at runtime.

--- a/src/Makefile.in
+++ b/src/Makefile.in
@@ -264,7 +264,7 @@
 top_build_prefix = @top_build_prefix@
 top_builddir = @top_builddir@
 top_srcdir = @top_srcdir@
-AM_CXXFLAGS = -Wall -std=c++11 -D_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 $(am__append_1)
+AM_CXXFLAGS = -Wall -std=c++11 -D_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 -static-libstdc++ -static-libgcc $(am__append_1)
 patchelf_SOURCES = patchelf.cc elf.h
 all: all-am
